{
 "_source": "BOM_Import_FBDI_Sequence_Mapping 1.xlsx, handed over 04-Aug-2026. One tab per interface, each listing the Oracle FBDI column order and the CSV column order side by side.",
 "_effective_date": "2026-08-04",
 "_analyst": [
  "'in BOM, FBDI sequence and CSV sequence are same' - verified here rather than assumed: the two columns of every tab were compared position by position and are identical, so ONE list serves both formats.",
  "'there is no END column in last for each row' - also verified: no tab lists an END column. This matters because the SUPPLIER bundle DOES append an END record terminator, and that behaviour must not be inherited here. A stray END shifts nothing but is an extra field Oracle does not expect on these interfaces."
 ],
 "_why_this_matters": "These are headerless CSVs. Column POSITION is the only thing carrying meaning, so a list that is right about the names and wrong about the order loads silently into the wrong fields.",
